  "visualVerdict": {
    "decision": "accept",
    "method": "Independent recognizable comparison of exact prior2e8265 embedded release and final2dd15ad at matched1280x800/390x844 generated-file/question/reply/unsent-draft states; retained exact fc77043 Relay screenshots and hash-validated official Zed explore reference support the scoped bar. No true blind study or feature-parity claim.",
    "findings": [
      "The final desktop Split keeps the prior quiet code-plus-AI appearance and sidebar width, while explicit Split/Tab choices and a named file/AI navigation row make both requested modes discoverable. The desktop navigation row costs40px of vertical source space; that tradeoff is visible and accepted for the new tab choice.",
      "Desktop Tab displays one wide AI surface or the editable file surface, with genuine tab roles, selected state, keyboard activation and arrow/Home navigation. The editor, chat, prompt and AI panel retain their original DOM identities through layout and project changes.",
      "Phone Tab keeps the prior full-width AI reading area and folds file/AI plus Split/Tab into the existing44px dock row. Phone Split is truly side-by-side; native typing, backward selection and both source scroll axes work at390x844,320x300 and844x390.",
      "At320x300, Split code content is119px wide and long source requires horizontal scrolling; a real tap changes to full-width File Tab. The shortest completed conversation region remains44px and running AI remains48px, with Stop, settings, composer and mode controls at least44px and hit-test reachable.",
      "The genuine prior Chromium4px clamp (110→106) is resolved: six cycles retain110 exactly, while a real native wheel in File Tab sets20 and AI→Split preserves20. WebKit retains110 and honors its native wheel result24.",
      "Project-local unsent prompts, source and conversation remain scoped while the device layout preference and working surface stay consistent. Existing desktop terminal state coordinates with both modes without a new shell, terminal input or AI turn during layout switches.",
      "Repeated switches retain the same bounded DOM; final15-cycle counts are465→465 in both browsers. Existing source/state bounds are reused, and the review adds no runtime dependency or product background job."
    ]
  },
